t met Peter  mccleave nearly three years ago he has  blood cancer and told us then that  without a stem cell transplant he had  seven years to live  but Peter's Southeast Asian Heritage  means it's harder for him to find a  genetic match today he's still waiting  if you are quite European then you've  got north of 70 chance of finding your  stem cell don't match but for any other  minority ethnic group your chances of  finding your life-saving match drop to  at best 37 I'm still looking for that  stem cell during a match I know they're  out there and often when you explain to  someone that you could potentially save  someone's life through nothing more than  a cheek swab it's not invasive it's not  painful  people engage because you understand  that actually there is a moment of  altruism right there where you could  potentially save someone's life if  plant  all are looking for a donor who could be  a stranger  who could save their life  Catherine ovato see Sky News
 

